-- title:
--   Lemma 6.4 — relative perturbation of absorbing chains with constant 4
-- statement:
--   Consider absorbing Markov chains $C$ and $\tilde C$ with an identical finite set of states $S'$, transition functions $\delta$ and $\tilde\delta$, and an absorbing state $\top$ (absorbing in both chains). Let
--   $$\eta=\max_{s,s'\in S'}\mathrm{rel}\big(\delta(s)(s'),\tilde\delta(s)(s')\big)\in[0,\infty].$$
--   Then for every state $s\in S'$,
--   $$|\mathrm{val}^C_\top(s)-\mathrm{val}^{\tilde C}_\top(s)|\le4|S'|\eta.$$
--
--   Together with Lemma 6.3 this bounds the error of truncating strategy probabilities independently of the discount factor.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: the probability measure on valid plays Ω_s generated by finite histories, strategies on valid histories → the Ionescu-Tulcea trajectory measure on all sequences in (S × A × B)^ℕ; strategies are defined on all finite stage lists; reason: invalid plays have probability zero and values of strategies on invalid histories never matter, so every expectation and value is unchanged
--   - encoding: a Markov chain C = (S, δ) → a game with both action sets Fin 1 (CSG n 1 1); its reachability value is the probability of reaching the target; reason: the source defines an MC as the special CSG where both players have one action
--   - encoding: rel(x, x') ∈ [0, ∞] with rel(x, 0) = rel(0, x) = ∞ for x > 0 → rel valued in ℝ≥0∞ (ENNReal); reason: the infinite case is represented exactly; no instance changes
--   - encoding: |val^C_⊤(s) − val^{C̃}_⊤(s)| ≤ 4|S'|η with η possibly ∞ → the inequality between ENNReal.ofReal |…| and 4·|S'|·η in ℝ≥0∞, S' = Fin k; reason: equivalent: for finite η it is the real inequality, for η = ∞ (with S' nonempty) both sides allow everything
-- source:
--   Ali Asadi, Krishnendu Chatterjee, The Computational Complexity of Concurrent Stochastic Games: Exact Value and Approximation, STOC 2027 submission #285 (October 2026), SHA-256 5cff187cf6b230b3bdfe540f2832f824d1ddb6acb43239fbf469d37c43b0d461, https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-1/285.pdf, Lemma 6.4 ([Sol03, Theorem 6]), printed p. 20 (PDF p. 22)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ConcurrentStochasticApprox_Approx_Game
import Definitions.Def_ConcurrentStochasticApprox_Approx_PowerSeries
open Finset

namespace ConcurrentStochasticApprox.Approx

/-- **Lemma 6.4.** Let `C, C̃` be absorbing Markov chains on the same finite state set `S'`, with
transition functions `δ, δ̃` and a common absorbing state `⊤`. Let
`η = max_{s,s' ∈ S'} rel(δ(s)(s'), δ̃(s)(s'))` (possibly `∞`). Then
`|val^C_⊤(s) - val^{C̃}_⊤(s)| ≤ 4 |S'| η` for every `s ∈ S'`. -/
theorem lemma_6_4 {k : ℕ} (C C' : CSG k 1 1) (top : Fin k) (hC : IsAbsorbingMC C)
    (hC' : IsAbsorbingMC C') (htop : IsAbsorbingState C top) (htop' : IsAbsorbingState C' top) :
    ∀ s, ENNReal.ofReal |reachValue C {top} s - reachValue C' {top} s| ≤
      4 * (k : ENNReal) * ⨆ s₀ : Fin k, ⨆ s' : Fin k, rel ((C.δ s₀ 0 0).1 s') ((C'.δ s₀ 0 0).1 s') := by sorry

end ConcurrentStochasticApprox.Approx
